</section>

<section class="acdt-intro content-section" aria-labelledby="intro-heading">
  <h2 id="intro-heading" class="sr-only">About British Summer Time Converter</h2>
  <p>
    Welcome to the premier standalone <strong>GMT to BST Converter</strong> on the internet. This specialized calculator is built for a single, focused purpose: converting Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) to British Summer Time (BST) with absolute precision. Please note that on this site, <strong>BST refers exclusively to British Summer Time</strong>—the daylight saving time offset (UTC+1) observed across the United Kingdom from late March to late October. It should not be confused with Bangladesh Standard Time (UTC+6), which is a separate time zone running 5 hours ahead of British Summer Time. By clearly defining this focus, we eliminate scheduling ambiguity for international teams, developers, and travelers.
  </p>
  <p>
    Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) represents the astronomical solar time reference computed at the Royal Observatory in Greenwich, London. Today, it aligns precisely with Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) at offset +0. GMT does not shift with the seasons, making it the perfect universal baseline for database architectures, financial markets, and aviation logs. However, because the UK shifts its local clocks to optimize sunlight during the summer months, scheduling meetings directly in GMT during summer can cause errors if you forget the clock change.
  </p>
  <p>
    This page is designed to help you navigate this transition. Whether you are a <strong>software developer</strong> syncing server logs in London with global endpoints, a <strong>financial trader</strong> timing trade windows on the London Stock Exchange, a <strong>freelancer</strong> coordinating delivery deadlines with British clients, a <strong>traveler</strong> preparing for a trip to the UK, or a <strong>student</strong> attending remote lectures from Scotland, Wales, or Northern Ireland, this page provides everything you need. With a minimum target of 5,000 words of original technical copy, we have structured this guide to offer unmatched informational depth, covering UK clock changes, meeting planning across five continents, and technical use cases.
  </p>
</section>

