<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     TIME DIFFERENCE SECTION & SIDE-BY-SIDE GRAPHIC
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section" id="time-difference" aria-labelledby="time-diff-heading">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Time Difference Mechanics</p>
    <h2 id="time-diff-heading">Analyzing the Time Gap: GMT vs BST</h2>
    <p>
      Understanding the difference between Greenwich Mean Time and British Summer Time comes down to a single mathematical factor: <strong>an offset of exactly +1 hour</strong>. GMT occupies the base position of UTC+0, while BST represents the daylight saving shift of UTC+1. When the daylight saving schedule is active in the United Kingdom, local clocks in London run 60 minutes ahead of the zero baseline.
    </p>
    <p>
      Daylight Saving Time (DST) exists to transfer morning daylight into the evening. By advancing clocks by 1 hour in late spring, the sunset occurs an hour later according to civil time, reducing domestic electricity consumption and providing extra recreational light in the evening. In winter, this offset is reverted so that morning daylight is restored during the coldest, darkest months, preventing children from walking to school in complete darkness.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Custom GMT vs BST Comparison Graphic (SVG) -->
  <div style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 700px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px;">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 600 200" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
      <!-- Main container -->
      <rect width="600" height="200" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
      
      <!-- Side by Side Visual Clocks -->
      <g transform="translate(100, 100)">
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="60" fill="#12455d" stroke="#2f6278" stroke-width="4" />
        <!-- Hand indicators -->
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-40" stroke="#f4fbff" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
