    <h2 id="meeting-heading">Meeting Planner: Connecting UK and Global Teams</h2>
    <p>
      Scheduling virtual calls between professionals working on Greenwich Mean Time (UTC+0), British Summer Time (UTC+1), and other global centers requires understanding overlap windows. Since BST is only 1 hour ahead of GMT, scheduling calls between these two zones is extremely easy. The complexity arises when coordinating multi-region calls that involve other markets like the US East Coast, Europe, India, or Australia.
